exports[`the MCP tool contracts deletePostTool keeps its contract 1`] = `
{
  "_meta": undefined,
  "annotations": {
    "destructiveHint": true,
    "idempotentHint": true,
    "openWorldHint": false,
    "readOnlyHint": false,
    "title": "Delete Post",
  },
  "description": "
Use this when the user wants to delete an existing post (scheduled, draft, published or errored).
Find the post first (list your posts) and pass its "id" here.
It deletes the post on that one channel together with its comments - a post created for several channels has a separate id on each channel.
A repeating post is listed once per repetition with the same id - deleting it deletes every repetition.
A deleted scheduled post is not published. Deleting a published post only removes it from Sharek - it stays live on the social network.
The deletion cannot be undone.
If the post cannot be deleted, the result contains output.errors explaining why.
",
  "inputSchema": {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "id": {
        "description": "The "id" of the post to delete",
        "type": "string",
      },
    },
    "required": [
      "id",
    ],
    "type": "object",
  },
  "name": "deletePostTool",
  "outputSchema": {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "output": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "postId": {
                "type": "string",
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "postId",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          {
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "errors": {
                "type": "string",
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "errors",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
        ],
      },
    },
    "required": [
      "output",
    ],
    "type": "object",
  },
}
`;

